    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51582" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zōrŏastres</span></b> , is,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Zoroaster</i>, <i>a lawgiver of the Medes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Just.
				1, 1, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 30, 1, 2, § 3</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. Mag. p.
			291</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Zōrŏ-astrēus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Zoroaster</i>, <i>Zoroastrian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">susurri,</span>”
				i. e. <i>magical</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Apoth. 494</span></i>
			 (where Zŏr-, by solecism).</div>
